    "evidence_text": "Spontaneous Combustion (album)\n\nShe Is Love (Parachute song)\n\n It was released on May 13, 2009.\n\n The album version was produced by Chris Keup/Stewart Myers.\n\n The full band version was produced by Kyle Kelso.\n\nDon't Call It Love\n\n Later the song was covered and released as a single by American entertainer Dolly Parton.\n\n It was released in January 1985 as the first single from the album \"Real Love\".\n\nLove Stinks (song)\n\n In Canada, the song reached number 15.\n\n Joan Jett covered the song for the soundtrack of the 1996 movie \"Mr. Wrong\".\n\n The song was also featured in the film \"Opie Gets Laid\".\n\nI Love You (The Zombies song)\n\"I Love You\" is a 1965 song by The Zombies, written by their member Chris White, which was covered by People!\n and The Carnabeats and by several other artists, including foreign translations.\n\nBetter Than Home\n\n One song on the album, \"Tell Her You Belong to Me\", took her a year and a half to write.\n\nI Saw the Light (Hank Williams song)\n\n.\n\n The song became the shows' closing song for Williams and one of his most popular tunes.\n\n Williams' version did not enjoy major success during its initial release.\n\n The song was soon covered by other acts and with time became a country gospel standard.\n\nCan We Talk\n\n It was the first single to be released from his double platinum second release \"I'm Ready\".\n\n The song was also Nominated for a Grammy Award for Best Rhythm & Blues Vocal Performance - Male.\n\n The song has also been covered by a Japanese/Korean singer during June 2008.\n\nChris White (musician)\n\nWillis Alan Ramsey (album)",
